From 370648518a3ac9f6dd0c1a295014e72149ea31fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:05:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 234/235] media: i2c: lc898214xd: sign extend the hall position
 readback

The position debugfs node printed the 12-bit hall reading unsigned, so
the whole negative half of the lens travel read back as 4019/3933/3828
instead of -77/-163/-268.

That node is the only instrument that distinguishes "the coil moved"
from "the target register accepted the write", and it was unreadable
exactly where the lens sits near its macro stop.

While here, record what a focus sweep measured on 2026-09-16, because it
contradicts the direction this file asserts: a farther subject is
sharpest at a HIGHER FOCUS_ABSOLUTE code, so code 0 focuses near rather
than at infinity, and a fit puts infinity near code 157 rather than 581.
The polarity is deliberately left alone for now -- libcamera's dioptre
map has to move in the same change, and the fit wants stations at
measured distances first.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
index f2f03f067b1a..f71475a423d3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/lc898214xd.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
  * 10} and {0xE0, BYTE_ADDR, 0x00, BYTE_DATA, MSM_ACT_POLL, 10}).
  */
 
+#include <linux/bitops.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
@@ -87,6 +88,28 @@
  * V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE is unsigned and, by convention, increases towards
  * near focus. So expose 0..581, mapping 0 -> +324 (infinity) and 581 -> -257
  * (macro), and convert on the way to the hardware.
+ *
+ * UNRESOLVED, measured 2026-09-16 (bringup/camera/af-sweep.py, exposure and
+ * scene stability both held, actuator readback tracking every step):
+ *
+ *   subject                 distance   sharpest at
+ *   lit book, square on     0.47 m     code 0    (9.3x over the range)
+ *   room, shelving          ~2-3 m     code 128  (up to 11x)
+ *   book on a far shelf     far        code 192  (15.5x)
+ *
+ * Sharpness rises with distance as the CODE rises, so pos 0 focuses NEAR and
+ * pos 581 FAR -- the opposite of both the labels above and the V4L2
+ * convention. A fit through the two solid points puts infinity near code 157,
+ * which would leave roughly two thirds of the exposed range beyond infinity
+ * and the near end unreachable (a subject at 0.155 m stayed flat to within
+ * 5% across the whole sweep, with no peak anywhere).
+ *
+ * That cannot be reconciled with the vendor's af_tuning (infinity +324, macro
+ * -257) without either those two fields being read swapped out of
+ * libactuator_lc898214xd.so, or the hall scale not being the DAC scale. The
+ * polarity is deliberately NOT flipped here yet: the tuning file's dioptre
+ * map would have to move in the same commit, and the fit needs stations at
+ * measured distances in daylight first.
  */
 #define LC898214XD_CODE_INFINITY	324
 #define LC898214XD_CODE_MACRO		(-257)
@@ -213,8 +236,14 @@ static int lc898214xd_position_show(struct seq_file *s, void *data)
 	if (lsb < 0)
 		return lsb;
 
-	seq_printf(s, "%u\n",
-		   ((msb << 8) | lsb) >> LC898214XD_CODE_SHIFT);
+	/*
+	 * The code is signed 12 bits, so sign extend it. Printed unsigned, the
+	 * whole negative half of the travel read back as 4019/3933/3828 rather
+	 * than -77/-163/-268, which makes the one instrument that proves the
+	 * coil moved unreadable exactly where the lens is near its macro stop.
+	 */
+	seq_printf(s, "%d\n",
+		   sign_extend32(((msb << 8) | lsb) >> LC898214XD_CODE_SHIFT, 11));
 
 	return 0;
 }
